<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sassacus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1560–<a href="/years/1637">1637</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sassacus was the grand sachem of the Pequot in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatobem">Tatobem</a> in the mid-1630s. He led the Pequot during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pequot-war">Pequot War</a> of 1636–1637 against the English colonists and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohegan">Mohegan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narragansett-people">Narragansett</a> allies. After the destruction of the Pequot fort at Mystic he fled west and was killed by the Mohawk, who sent his head to the English.</p></div>
